></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ceolred-of-mercia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ceolred-of-mercia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ceolred of Mercia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ceolred was king of Mercia from 709 to 716, the son of Æthelred.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ceolwulf-ii-of-mercia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ceolwulf-ii-of-mercia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ceolwulf II of Mercia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ceolwulf II was king of Mercia from 874 to about 879, installed by the Great Heathen Army after Burgred fled.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cephissus-boeotia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cephissus-boeotia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cephissus (Boeotia)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cephissus is a river of central Greece that rises near Mount Parnassus in Phocis and flows east through Phocis and Boeotia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/cerasus"><span class="enc-name">Cerasus</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Cerasus was an ancient Greek city on the southern Black Sea coast of Anatolia, founded as a colony of Sinope; its site is usually placed at or near modern Giresun in…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/cerball-mac-dunlainge"><span class="enc-name">Cerball mac Dúnlainge</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cerball mac Dúnlainge was king of Osraige in Ireland from about 842 until his death in 888.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cercamon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/t